		{"id":"1e43f359e9105b57","x":-480,"y":-40,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"1","type":"text","text":"## Visual Navigation through 3DGS"},
		{"id":"716b3100f7895af5","x":-60,"y":-360,"width":215,"height":400,"type":"text","text":"### Direct Path Planning on 3DGS primitives\n***\nInstead of converting 3DGS to voxel/grid maps for planning, directly plan paths using Gaussian primitives. Key gap: Existing methods rasterize 3DGS to grids before planning, losing explicit geometric information. Opportunity: Develop collision checking and cost functions directly on Gaussian covariances for efficient planning.\n\nhttps://novix.science/search-v1/5192ee353e581cea4547d7a5c53f46a7?isNewSession=true&hadExplicitAgent=true&initialAgentName=Idea%20Agent"},
		{"id":"26cefd316b047b5c","x":-480,"y":200,"width":250,"height":120,"color":"1","type":"text","text":"## 3D Gaussian Splatting with Language Understanding"},
